{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["And he mentioned here, <b>and they took possession of his land and the land of Og king of Bashan from Aroer, etc.</b> The reason is that he returned to mention what he said at the beginning of this book (Deuteronomy 1:4), for the exposition of this Torah was after striking Sihon king of the Amorites, who dwelt in Heshbon, and Og king of Bashan, who dwelt in Ashtaroth in Edrei. And he added here to explain that the exposition was also after they had taken possession of all their land — that is to say, that he distributed it to them to the two tribes and the half-tribe."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:45:48.674367021Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}